Lets GeoJSONSource::setOverrideSynchronousUpdate() turn synchronous updates
off as well as on, and makes a change reach the tiles a source already has. A
source reported options->synchronousUpdate || overrideSynchronousUpdate, so one
whose options or style JSON set "synchronousUpdate": true stayed synchronous
whatever the override said. The override now replaces the option once it is
set. A tile also lays out in the mode it was created with, and
RenderGeoJSONSource reuses its tiles when the data changes, so a mode change
didn't reach them. RenderGeoJSONSource now recreates its tiles when the mode
changes (https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/1491).

Recreating the tiles leaves the old tiles' queued background slices to run. If
the source turned synchronous, the new tiles then slice the same geojson-vt
index inline on the render thread, while GeoJSONVT::getTile() fills its tile
cache without synchronization. Turning synchronous updates on while a slice ran
already raced the same way. GeoJSONVTData now holds a mutex around every
slice. Supercluster indexes need none, since their queries are const and never
change the index after construction.
Upstream: not proposed

